    "name": "count-max-the-scope-and-the-levels-list-intersect",
    "why": "FOUND BY A PLANT THAT STAYED GREEN. Deleting `personInScope` from this type changed nothing across the whole corpus, because no count case set CG-01's scope at all — the fifth-plant shape of P2-1's review finding, in the first type of P2-2. Owner decision K's actual sentence is that a bare `levels` list INTERSECTS the scope rather than replacing it, and an intersection needs three people to pin: p-ali is an R1 on PICU and is judged, p-noor is an R1 on NICU whom the scope excludes, and p-zaid is an R2 on PICU whom the levels list excludes. All three hold three duties against a cap of two, so each filter is the only thing between clean and flagged for its own person, and dropping either one flags somebody it should not.",
